 pay anything and even  though this is a recipe for disaster you  can see coming from a mile away it was  still pretty freaky when she had to  produce her first payment by puking up a  newborn kitten from there she goes  through a series of spells that  predictably cost her more than what she  gains especially at the beginning it's  going much worse for her than it is for  lou and that is the setup she's lost the  only thing she cares about she wants  revenge against the mentor turned  predator and that drives her to borrow  who you'll learn later is also a  parasite  eventually the curse starts to kick in  and things start to fall apart for luke  but there is a twist along the way  that's important for the ending after  lou loses his son who winds up as one of  boro's zombie minions who she keeps  around and animated with a tadpole  smoothie concoction he finds out where  the witch lives through the incompetent  henchmen he poached from lisa when he  goes to see her instead of trying to  protect lisa she seems happy to help him  there were plenty of red flags before  this but it becomes clear that she wants  something more from lisa than just her  kittens she tells him that she isn't  sure what but that something happened  when they were making the movie and that  he should go look into it he makes his  way to the house in the woods where she  made the film and he meets the actress  who played lucy who's actually missing  her eye and is pretty pissed off at lisa  it turns out that they were lovers and  that she actually financed the short and  in an effort to deliver an amazing  performance she decided to take some  peyote and that led to the creation of  this amazing last scene that everyone  had been hinting at but we hadn't really  seen yet it turns out that she gouged  her own eye out and then ate it on  camera so while everyone thought that  lisa was this fantastic filmmaker it  wasn't special effects or some kind of  directorial wizardry that they were  watching although it does sound like  there was some raw talent on display in  front of and behind the camera what  really made it such a memorable piece  was this incredible sacrifice that mary  made on screen she couldn't remember  what happened and she never saw the film  so before lou left he offered to screen  it for her and gave her his number  finding out that lisa's exploiting this  to get a feature made means that mary  has a huge resentment against her and  heads to la to see what happened to her  eye  as you get to the end you learn that  boro is hundreds of years old and she  did something in the past a long time  ago that she can't take back after  finding out that the body she currently  occupies was once a pretty normal woman  named jennifer who had a husband and  kids you learn that the entity's  longevity is accomplished by jumping  from one body to another  it all started in brazil about 900 years  ago which is interesting because that's  also where lisa spent her childhood boro  started out as a man and one day he  encountered a huge stunning white jaguar  in the forest she described it as like  the mother jaguar a spirit living in an  animal body the jaguar likes the man and  they hook up and she leaves him with  some of her power as a reward he uses  that to become a king and he marries  this great princess and he just has to  give the jaguar an offering of a  sacrifice every so often then his  kingdom comes under threat and he needs  the jaguar again she tells him to go  looking for the poison toad when she  licks it she's able to see where her  enemies are and set a trap but this time  the jaguar wants a big sacrifice in  return she tells the king to bring her  his wife in an attempt to trick the  jaguar he brings a different woman and  that doesn't work out knowing she's been  betrayed the jaguar comes and eats his  wife anyways and then mauls the male  burrow leaving him for dead a young girl  finds him as he's dying alone in the  forest and without even knowing that he  could he uses the last of his strengths  to jump into her body he's been doing  that ever since as far as boro knows the  jaguar was killed by the spanish and  then turned into a couch as soon as lisa  hears that she realizes it's the one  that she saw at the bottom of the ladder  under the trap door that appeared in her  room boro says the jaguar still lives  but is just on the other side and we'll  come back to that  by the time you make it to the finale  lisa has been through a lot she's  produced quite a few kittens including  one that she birthed out of a new  orifice that appeared on her side after  she said she didn't want to puke them  out anymore  she went to jail after eating  psychedelic guinea pig stew she was  choked to death only to be brought back  which was an extra brutal scene because  it was cut with mary watching the film  where you finally see the scene with her  eye for the first time and on top of  that all of her friends code his  girlfriend christine and her movie star  sort of boyfriend roy hardaway all end  up dead she does succeed in ruining  lou's life though after she got him to  snort a worm that she found on a flower  from the vine that was taking over her  entire apartment building it grew inside  his head it damaged both of his optic  nerves and he was left blind after she  removed it before that she had gone to  his hotel intending to kill him but  after he admitted the fact that he took  the movie away because she made him feel  small when she moved his hand off her  thigh she realized that it wasn't really  worth it to kill him while she was  dealing with all that she was constantly  getting stronger and you started to put  it together that what boro really wanted  was her body and that the whole  backstory of lisa's mom leaving when she  was a baby well that's not really what  happened after lisa licked the toad boro  told her that she'd die in about six  hours if she didn't do rituals and sex  and blood magic she does the first with  roy but can't go through with the second  because it involves eating an omelette  with some of code's flesh inside she  refuses saying that she feels like she  traded his life for her movie and while  she walks away the creepy looking shadow  entity that's been popping up comes  right up and touches her the implication  here is that it's protecting her and  removing the poison and when it's done  it attacks borrow leaving her injured  and unconscious on the couch the uncle  comes in to try to finish the job of  killing lisa and she has to use the trap  door to try to get away from him there  she sees the couch again recognizes it's  the jaguar and tells it that she  betrayed you talking about borrow and  says you've been looking for her all  this time then the faceless woman from  her dreams appears and she makes the  connection that part of what's inside of  her comes from the jaguar they talk and  she realizes it's her mother and when  she asks to see her face  you realize it's that entity that she's  seeing even though she doesn't need to  hear it her mother tells her that boro  will betray her she explains the kittens  she says that borrow's using those to  steal her blood from lisa's body without  that she's weak and for lisa to go do  what she needs to do and then come find  her so in the end she does get her  revenge she gets the movie back she  meets with alvin sender he says that  he'll draw up a new contract and she's  guaranteed to direct after everything  she's been through and her talk with the  jaguar she's able to stop boro from  jumping into her body she knows better  than to make a deal with her and is even  able to stop her bringing forth another  kitten and so boro has to settle for  jumping into mary's body which we see  her do instead of sticking around in la  and making the movie lisa nova buys  herself a ticket to brazil where we can  expect that she's going to try to find  her mother i found the show to be an 